    <string name="cs_title">Share a coarse summary with the cloud?</string>
    <string name="cs_sent_h">WHAT IS SENT (to DeepInfra, only when you tap Ask):</string>
    <string name="cs_sent_b">• Total assets rounded to 2 significant figures\n• Available / reserved / earning as whole percentages\n• Lending lines: protocol, asset symbol, share, APR\n• Bills grouped by due window: count and rounded total\n• Last 30 days of cash flow by fixed category: rounded totals\n• Days of runway, and the question you type</string>
    <string name="cs_never_h">WHAT IS NEVER SENT:</string>
    <string name="cs_never_b">• Private keys, seed phrases, your API key\n• Wallet or contract addresses, transaction hashes\n• Invoice IDs, counterparty names, memos, category labels\n• Exact balances or amounts, exact dates\n• Anything the privacy filter does not recognise</string>
    <string name="cs_foot">The cloud model is read-only: it returns advice text only and cannot move or approve funds. You can inspect every payload in the activity log and turn this off at any time. DeepInfra says it does not store prompts or outputs; Google and Anthropic models are blocked because those providers do.</string>
    <string name="cs_accept">I understand — enable</string>
    <string name="cs_decline">Keep local only</string>
